diff --git a/docs/linked-expenses.md b/docs/linked-expenses.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3400627
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/linked-expenses.md
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+# Linked itinerary and expenses
+
+An itinerary card describes a place/activity; a private `misc` expense describes a payment. `misc.itineraryId` links them by stable item ID. Multiple payments can link to one card. Name and date are copied when starting a new payment, then remain the payment's historical description/date: renaming or rescheduling the itinerary does not silently rewrite the ledger.
+
+## Use
+
+- In the itinerary editor, **儲存並記花費** saves the card and opens a payment with name/date already filled. Existing cards have **記花費** and a count/summary of linked payments.
+- In a payment, **連結行程** can select an existing card or **＋ 同時新增行程**. Creating both uses the payment name/date and optional itinerary time, category and URL. A journey date is required; selecting an existing card never overwrites an existing payment's description or historical date.
+- The new card has an empty budget, no private payment note, and no copied amount. Its actual payment is counted once through `misc`; explicit itinerary budgets remain separate estimates. Cash/card, currency, actual TWD, receipts and wallet behavior retain their existing semantics.
+- Unlinking or deleting either side does not delete the other side. Missing cards are labeled rather than hiding payments. Exchange/cashflow records do not create itinerary links.
+
+## Durability and privacy
+
+Creating both commits the two documents plus outbox entries in one IndexedDB transaction. Draft IDs are stable during retries. Cloud upload retains the existing per-document idempotent operations and revision conflicts; it is eventual synchronization, not an atomic multi-document server transaction. A temporary missing link remains readable while the second document is pending or conflicted. Backups preserve IDs and links without a migration.
+
+The public itinerary projection retains its strict field allowlist; it never follows `misc` links. Payment amounts, notes, receipts, balances and the links themselves are excluded. Linked spending summaries/buttons render only for the owner.
+
+## Validation
+
+28 cloud/collaboration tests pass, including linked offline writes, restart/retry after a lost response, second-device convergence, no duplicate records, no copied budget, privacy and independent deletion. The existing 28 segment/money/wallet tests are run separately. Local browser testing covers creating both from a payment, recording multiple payments from one card, and saving a new itinerary directly into its prefilled payment form. Physical phone/tablet airplane-mode testing remains a user trial check.
